# fs-smoke

A portable application that mounts the board's own storage at "/data" with
mm.fs.local, runs mm.fs.conformance's checks inside it, prints a line per
result on the console, and unmounts. It names no board, SDK, or file system:
on Linux the storage is the device map's directory.0, or the working
directory, and the checks leave nothing behind in it.

It skips, exiting 0, when mm.fs.local answers Unsupported or NotFound.

Exit codes:

| Code | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Every check passed, or there is no local storage and the run skipped. |
| 1 | Mounting failed for another reason. |
| 2 | The checks could not run: the scratch directory could not be made. |
| 3 | Unmounting failed. |
| 4 | At least one check failed; the console names the first. |
